1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,480
Who decides the school future of
kids with a foreign background?

2
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:06,877
We often think they end
up in vocational schools

3
00:00:06,877 --> 00:00:09,460
because of low grades or financial pressure.

4
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:14,160
But this school segregation
hides a much subtler mechanism.

5
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:19,780
Take an excellent immigrant student with the
same maths grades as his Italian classmate.

6
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:23,100
At the start of middle school,
they're on the same track.

7
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,920
Yet, when the final choice comes,
the path inexplicably forks

8
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:32,100
and the immigrant student
is diverted downwards.

9
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:35,760
The first real obstacle is
invisible, it's internal.

10
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:41,540
Held back by social barriers, these kids
lower their aspirations and limit themselves.

11
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:45,880
But targeted guidance can
unlock their ambition.

12
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:47,900
And this is where the domino effect kicks in.

13
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:52,900
When teachers notice this new
confidence and turn their advice around,

14
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:57,520
instead of suggesting vocational school,
they open the doors to the liceo.

15
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:03,040
By aligning inner ambition with outside
expectations, the gap disappears.

16
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:07,100
So that bright kid stops doubting himself

17
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:10,700
and heads straight for the liceo
he deserved from the start.

